// Title: ESXi Account Creation Via ESXCLI
// Sigma ID: b28e4eb3-8bbc-4f0c-819f-edfe8e2f25db
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Cedric Maurugeon
// Date: 2023-08-22 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, execution, T1136, T1059.012
// Description: Detects user account creation on ESXi system via esxcli
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administration activities
// References:
//   - https://developer.broadcom.com/xapis/esxcli-command-reference/7.0.0/namespace/esxcli_system.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_esxcli_user_account_creation.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/esxcli" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "system " and ProcessCommandLine contains "account " and ProcessCommandLine contains "add ")
